# Lines the country test (country.bat) must write to COM1 with
# COUNTRY=044,850,A:\COUNTRY.SYS (scripts/smoke-test): the United Kingdom
# in code page 850, from the file given. The currency is the pound sign,
# 9Ch in code pages 437 and 850. CHCP 850 keeps the code page.

^GRDOS-TEST-BEGIN$
^== COUNTRY$
^COUNTRY 044 DATE 1 TIME 0 CURRENCY "\x9C" FORMAT 0 DIGITS 2$
^SEPARATORS THOUSANDS "," DECIMAL "\." DATE "-" TIME ":" LIST ","$
^CODEPAGE ACTIVE 850 SYSTEM 437$
^UPCASE 84 41$
^Current date is \w{3} \d\d-\d\d-\d{4}$
^Enter new date \(dd-mm-yy\): $
^Current time is +\d+:\d\d:\d\d\.\d\d[ap]$
^NLSINFO  COM +544 \d\d-\d\d-\d\d +\d+:\d\d[ap]$
^== NLSFUNC$
^Active code page: 850$
^Active code page: 850$
^COUNTRY 044 DATE 1 TIME 0 CURRENCY "\x9C" FORMAT 0 DIGITS 2$
^CODEPAGE ACTIVE 850 SYSTEM 437$
^GRDOS-TEST-END$
